   174	Give these spine variables the weights
   175	`wt(c_j)=wt(u_j)=j` and `wt(b2)=2t+1`.
   176	After weights `<j` have been solved, let `rho_j` be
   177	`[X^(4t+1-j)]R` with `z_j=0`.  Weighted homogeneity proves that this row is
   178	independent of every later variable and is affine in `z_j`: a later variable
   179	has weight greater than `j`, while `z_j^2` has weight greater than `j`.
   180	Therefore the exact induction is
   181	
   182	```text
   183	z_j=-rho_j/p_j.                                       (2.9)
