   455	### 5.2 Why the proposed affine triangle is not yet present
   456	
   457	In the residual auxiliaries every original top row is nonlinear in every
   458	original variable.  The exact per-variable degrees, with entries ordered by
   459	ascending band, are
   460	
   461	| `t` | variables | degree vectors by band |
   462	|---:|---|---|
   463	| 3 | `(b3,u2)` | `(2,5),(2,4),(2,4)` |
   464	| 4 | `(b3,u2,u3)` | `(2,6,4),(2,6,4),(2,5,3),(2,5,3)` |
   465	| 5 | `(b3,u2,u3,u4)` | `(2,8,5,4),(2,7,5,3),(2,7,4,3),(2,6,4,3),(2,6,4,3)` |
   466	
   467	Thus no permutation of the original rows and variables even has an initial
   468	affine-unit pivot.  Modular subsystem audits on one `H_t` fibre give the
   469	following zero-dimensional lengths after the first `t-1` rows; only adding
   470	the final row produces `[1]`:
   471	
   472	| `t` | ascending bands | descending bands |
   473	|---:|---:|---:|
   474	| 3 | 10 | 8 |
   475	| 4 | 57 | 44 |
   476	| 5 | 298 | 224 |
   477	
   478	Removing any one top row at `t=3,4,5` also leaves a nonzero zero-dimensional
   479	ideal; at `t=5` this leave-one-out check was repeated on both fibres.  Thus
   480	none of these records supplies the requested induction "one
   481	original row introduces one auxiliary with a unit affine coefficient".  A
   482	nonlinear triangular change may exist, but it has not been derived.  Calling
   483	the final Gröbner reduction a uniform triangle would violate the indexed-
   484	recurrence guardrail.
   485	
   486	### 5.3 Exact determinant reduction of the open step
   487	
   488	Put `F_r=T_(t,t+r)|_(b4=1)` for `0<=r<t`, choose
   489	the cheaper measured prefix `J_t=<F_1,...,F_(t-1)>`, and set
   490	`B_t=A_t[b3,u_2,...,u_(t-1)]/J_t`.  If `B_t` is first proved finite over
   491	`A_t`, the finite-algebra multiplication criterion gives, componentwise in
   492	the separable rank-two algebra,
   493	
   494	```text
   495	<F_0,...,F_(t-1)>=[1]
   496	 iff multiplication by F_0 on B_t is bijective
   497	 iff Delta_t=det(mu_(F_0)) is a unit in A_t.           (5.2)
   498	```
   499	
   500	At a split index the two determinants must be checked at `d=+s,-s`; one may
   501	not invert their product in advance.  For a displayed class
   502	`Delta_t=a_t d+b_t`, the single split-safe norm condition is
   503	`4q^2(3b_t^2-a_t^2(t+1))!=0`.  What remains is exactly
   504	
   505	```text
   506	OPEN[TOP-TAIL-DETERMINANT-RECURRENCE]:
   507	 prove B_t finite, construct an indexed A_t-basis and recurrence for Delta_t,
   508	 and prove its norm has no admissible integer zero.                  (5.3)
   509	```
   510	
   511	The fixed lengths `8,44,224` at `t=3,4,5` do not prove the first clause
   512	uniformly; no extrapolation from those three values is made.
   513	
   514	## 6. `RESIDUAL-ZERO`
   515	
   303	## 3. Replay
   304	
   305	Every Singular job ran under `timeout`, in four parallel streams, on a host at
   306	load average ~45; the batch was blocked on to completion inside this turn and
   307	nothing was left running.  `jplus_hom.py` reproduces the ring, weights, minpoly,
   308	variable order and generator list of the charged `analyze_rows.py` verbatim and
   309	adds the homogeneity assertions of 2.4.
   310	
   311	| `t` | fibre / prime | `JPLUS dim` | GB size | time (s) | pure powers in `lead` | typing |
   312	|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---|---|
   313	| 2 | `y=1/5` exact | **1** | 3 | <1 | `b4^7` only, **no `b3` power** | negative control, matches |
   314	| 2 | `y=1/5` mod 32003 | **1** | 3 | <1 | `b4^7` only | negative control, matches |
   315	| 2 | `y=2/5` exact | **0** | 3 | <1 | `b3^2, b4^8` | matches |
   316	| 3 | `Q(sqrt3)` exact | **0** | 15 | <1 | `b3^2, b4^10, q2^8` | matches |
   317	| 4 | `Q(sqrt15)` exact | **0** | 66 | 21 | `b3^2, b4^12, q2^9, q3^8` | matches |
   318	| 4 | mod 32029, `r=25378` | **0** | 66 | <1 | identical to exact | **agreement control** |
   319	| 4 | mod 32029, `r=31563` | **0** | 66 | <1 | identical to exact | **agreement control** |
   320	| 5 | mod 32009, `r=1821` | **0** | 285 | <1 | `b3^2,b4^14,q2^10,q3^9,q4^8` | certificate |
   321	| 5 | mod 32009, `r=15639` | **0** | 285 | <1 | identical | certificate |
   322	| 6 | mod 32003, `r=27617` | **0** | 1224 | 12 | `b3^2,b4^16,q2^11,q3^10,q4^9,q5^8` | certificate |
   323	| 7 | mod 32059, `r=4425` | **0** | 5304 | 1152 | `b3^2,b4^18,q2^13,q3^11,q4^10,q5^9,q6^9` | certificate |
   324	
   325	Every certificate line carries a pure power of **every** variable in `lead(G)`,
   326	so the special fibre's `Proj` is empty by the ideal-theoretic criterion of 1.2,
   327	independently of Singular's `dim` in a `wp` ring; at `t=2, y=1/5` `b3` has **no**
   328	pure power, in exact and modular arithmetic alike -- the lemma's contrapositive
   329	behaving correctly.  The `t=4` exact/modular agreement (same dim, same GB size
   330	66, same lead ideal, rows matching term by term) is the positive control for the
   331	whole promotion.  The charged `analyze_rows.py` battery at `t=2` reproduces the
   332	banked table exactly: `y=1/5` -- `dim 1`, `T0HOM power 1`, `RESZ dim 1`,
   333	`TOPT b4^7`, both charts `UNIT`; `y=2/5` -- `dim 0`, `T0HOM power 1`,
   334	`RESZ dim 0`, `TOPT b4^10`, both charts `UNIT`.
   335	
   336	**Scope of the promotion.**  With (H-int),(H-gen),(H-hom),(H-loud) confirmed and
   337	the lemma of 1.3, each `dim = 0` line above is a characteristic-zero proof that
   338	`V(I_(t,+)) = {0}` over `Abar_t`, hence of (8.1), hence -- through the banked,
   339	uniformly proved reduction chain -- of (T) at that `t`.  For non-split `t` one
   340	root suffices (the two roots are the two embeddings of the quadratic field
   341	`A_t`; `V(J.K[x]) = {0}` is a statement about `K = A_t` and is
   342	embedding-independent); both roots were run at `t=4,5` as redundancy.
   343	**PROVED: `t = 3, 4, 5, 6, 7`** (`t=2` is exact and needs no promotion; it
   344	satisfies (8.1) on both fibres but (V0) only on `y=2/5`).
   345	**NOT PROVED: `t = 8, 9, 11` (INCONCLUSIVE_TIMEOUT) and every `t >= 12`.**
   346	
   347	## 4. Reconciliation with Lemma CONE
   348	
   349	* **(V0) `<=>` `dim I_(t,+) = 0`.**  `I_(t,+)` is generated by weighted
   350	  homogeneous polynomials of positive weight, so `Z_+ = V(I_(t,+))` is stable
   351	  under the `G_m`-action and contains `0`; a `G_m`-stable set is finite iff it
   352	  is `{0}`, and `dim` of the affine quotient is `0` iff `Z_+` is finite.  This
   353	  is Opus's (1.1) and Fable's (V0) verbatim.  TYPED: **the two lemmas state the
   354	  same condition**; CONFIRMED.
   355	* **Opus's tau-criterion is the exact statement, and is strictly weaker.**
   356	  Lemma CONE gives `(8.1) <=> tau_t in sqrt(I_(t,+))` (necessary and
   357	  sufficient) with Corollary C1 `dim I_(t,+) = 0 => (8.1)` (sufficient only).
   358	  The strictness is witnessed at `t=2, y=1/5` and was verified here rather than
   359	  cited: `JPLUS dim = 1` (so (V0) FAILS) while `T0HOM_IN_RADICAL power=1` and
   360	  both charts are `UNIT` (so (8.1) HOLDS).  TYPED: CONFIRMED.
   361	* Consequently the promotion lemma proves the **stronger** statement (V0) and
   362	  gets (8.1) as a corollary.  A future `t` with `dim I_(t,+) > 0` would not
   363	  refute (8.1); it would put that `t` outside the reach of this instrument, and
   364	  the fallback would be the radical membership `tau_t in sqrt(I_(t,+))`.  That
   365	  fallback is **not** promotable by the lemma of 1.3, and not for a soft reason:
   366	  radical membership modulo `P` does not lift.  Take `R = Z_(p)`, `n = 2`,
   367	  `wt x = wt y = 1`, `J = (x - p y)`, `tau = x`.  Then `x` vanishes on
   368	  `V(J.kappa[x]) = {x=0}`, so `tau in sqrt(J.kappa[x])`; but on
   369	  `V(J.K[x]) = {x = p y}` one has `x = p != 0`, so `tau not-in sqrt(J.K[x])`.
   370	  The lemma promotes emptiness of a proper special fibre, and the locus
   371	  `V(I_(t,+)) cap D(tau_t)` whose emptiness is at issue is **open**, not
   372	  proper.  TYPED: OPEN, flagged.
   373	
   374	## 5. Side finding: the lead-ideal pattern is refuted at `t=7`
   375	
   376	The producer records, typed MEASURED, that `lead I_(t,+)` contains `b3^2`,
   377	`b3 b4^(t+2)`, `b4^(2t+4)` and `q_(j,0)^(t+7-j)`, offering the last as the finite
   378	evidence for the uniform target of its section 8.  Measured here: at `t=2..6`
   379	predicted = measured; at `t=7` `b4^18 = b4^(2t+4)` still holds, but the exponents
   380	are `q_2^13` (predicted 12) and `q_6^9` (predicted 8) -- **pattern refuted at
   381	`t=7`**.  Nothing is retracted (it was typed MEASURED, never promoted), but the
   382	stated evidence for a `q_(t-1,0)`-pure-power uniform statement is weaker than the
   383	report suggests.  TYPED: MEASURED, refuting the extrapolation.
   384	
