The new exact-order computations agree across both roots modulo 1009 through \(t=6\), and exact \(t=3,4\) agrees with modular data. The \(A_t\)-lengths so far are \(66,338,1709,8621\). The initial pure-power exponents differ sharply from the banked legacy order, confirming that the requested full `wp` tie-break must be declared explicitly. I’m moving to the expensive \(t=7,8\) cases now.
