Emit small analysis wrappers around a preexpanded K=16 cone job. The input is
an existing ``.sing`` file containing declarations ``T0,...``. Only the
coefficient field/minpoly and those polynomial declarations are copied; the
original computation at the end of the file is deliberately not copied. In
particular, this script never invokes Singular. The two built-in variable
orders use the same weighted grading: ``requested``
``(b4,q2_0,...,q(t-1)_0,b3), wp(1,2,...,t-1,t+1)``. ``legacy``
``(b3,b4,q2_0,...,q(t-1)_0), wp(t+1,1,2,...,t-1)``. Each emitted job is meant
to be run separately, in the foreground, e.g. ``timeout 1800 Singular -q
JOB.sing``. Keeping the engines in separate jobs means that a timeout in one
engine does not hide the other trials.

positional arguments:
  source                preexpanded cone .sing source

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --t T                 explicit t (also cross-checked)
  --order {requested,legacy}
  --variant {direct,incremental,groebner,slimgb,target,all}
                        one engine, or all independent engine jobs (target
                        only if supplied)
  --pure-bound PURE_BOUND
  --output OUTPUT       output .sing path for one variant
  --out-dir OUT_DIR
  --hilbert-numerator HILBERT_NUMERATOR
                        known numerator as comma/space-separated integers
  --hilbert-numerator-file HILBERT_NUMERATOR_FILE
                        file containing only an intvec or comma/space-
                        separated integers
  --check-only          parse and structurally validate every selected
                        emission without writing
