codex
The literal \(t+2\)-row test is now computationally confirmed through \(t=6\): its Hilbert numerator never equals the proposed complete-intersection product (lengths \(66,359,2001,11354\)). The dimension obstruction already proves this for every \(t\). After correcting the cardinality to \(t\), the tail rows \(T_t,\ldots,T_{2t-1}\) are regular sequences through \(t=6\), with CI lengths \(90,572,3640,23256\).
