codex
The computational bottleneck is exactly where the algebra predicts it: the original row leaders all point in the \(b_4\) direction, so the pure powers for the other variables arise only after many \(S\)-polynomials. This rules out the hoped-for pairwise-coprime leading-row proof even if every pure-\(b_4\) coefficient is nonzero.
